#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:12
msgid "Constant Head Tanks"
msgstr "Tanques de carga constante"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:18
msgid "Flow :math:`Q` and Water Level :math:`h` as a Function of Time"
msgstr "El caudal :math:`Q` y el nivel del agua :math:`h` en función del tiempo"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:20
msgid ""
"Our first step is to see if we can get constant head out of a simple system."
" The most simple flow control system is a bucket or tank with a hole in it. "
"This system is too coarse to provide constant head. One step above that is a"
" bucket or tank with a valve. This is where we begin our search for constant"
" head."
msgstr ""
"Nuestro primer paso es determinar si podemos obtener una carga constante con un sistema "
"sencillo. El sistema de control de flujo más sencillo es un cubo o tanque "
"con un orificio. Este sistema es demasiado rudimentario para proporcionar una carga "
"constante. Una opción algo mejor es un cubo o tanque con una "
"válvula. Aquí es donde comenzamos nuestra búsqueda de carga constante."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:22
msgid ""
"Using the setup described in the image below, we derive the following "
"equation for flow :math:`Q` through the valve as a function of time "
":math:`t`. The derivation is found here: "
":ref:`heading_flow_for_a_tank_with_a_valve`."
msgstr ""
"Con la configuración descrita en la siguiente imagen, derivamos la "
"ecuación para el caudal :math:`Q` a través de la válvula en función"
" del tiempo :math:`t`. La derivación se encuentra aquí: "
":ref:`heading_flow_for_a_tank_with_a_valve`."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:30
msgid "Drip hypochlorinator variables"
msgstr "Variables de hipocloración por goteo"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:30
msgid "This figure shows the variables that are defined in the equation above."
msgstr "Esta figura muestra las variables definidas en la ecuación anterior."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:32
msgid ""
"This equation has historically given students some trouble, and while its "
"nuances are explained in the derivation, they will be quickly summarized "
"here:"
msgstr ""
"Esta ecuación ha causado históricamente algunos problemas a los estudiantes "
"y, aunque sus detalles se explican en la derivación, aquí se resumen "
"rápidamente:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:34
msgid ""
":math:`t_{Design}` is **NOT** the time it takes to drain the tank. It is the"
" time that it *would* take to drain the tank *if* the flow rate at time "
":math:`t = 0`, :math:`Q_0`, were the flow rate forever, which it is not. "
":math:`t_{Design}` was used in the derivation to simplify the equation, "
"which is why this potentially-confusing parameter exists. The actual time it"
" takes to drain the tank lies somewhere between :math:`t_{Design}` and "
":math:`2 \\, t_{Design}` and depends on the ratio "
":math:`\\frac{h_{Tank}}{h_0}`."
msgstr ""
":math:`t_{Design}` **NO** es el tiempo que tarda el tanque en vaciarse. Es el "
"tiempo que *tardaría* en vaciarse *si* el caudal en :math:`t = 0`, "
":math:`Q_0`, permaneciera constante indefinidamente, lo cual no sucede. "
":math:`t_{Design}` se utilizó en la derivación para simplificar la ecuación; "
"de ahí la existencia de este parámetro, que puede resultar confuso. El tiempo "
"real de vaciado se encuentra entre :math:`t_{Design}` y "
":math:`2 \, t_{Design}`, y depende de la relación "
":math:`\\frac{h_{Tank}}{h_0}`."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:35
msgid ""
":math:`h_{Tank}` is not the same as :math:`h_{0}`. :math:`h_{Tank}` is the "
"height of water level in the tank with reference to the tank bottom. "
":math:`h_{0}` is the water level in the tank with reference to the valve. "
"Neither change with time, they both refer to the water level at one instance"
" in time, :math:`t = 0`. Therefore, :math:`h_{0} \\geq h_{Tank}` is always "
"true. If the tank is elevated far above the valve, then the :math:`h_{0} > >"
" h_{Tank}`. If the valve is at the same elevation as the bottom of the tank,"
" then :math:`h_{0} = h_{Tank}`. Please refer to the figure above to clarify "
":math:`h_{0}` and :math:`h_{Tank}`."
msgstr ""
":math:`h_{Tank}` no es igual a :math:`h_{0}`. :math:`h_{Tank}` es la "
"altura del agua en el tanque medida desde el fondo. "
":math:`h_{0}` es el nivel del agua en el tanque medido con respecto a la "
"válvula. Ninguno varía con el tiempo; ambos corresponden al nivel del agua "
"en el instante :math:`t = 0`. Por lo tanto, :math:`h_{0} "
"\\geq h_{Tank}` siempre se cumple. Si el tanque está muy elevado por "
"encima de la válvula, entonces :math:`h_{0} > > h_{Tank}`. Si la válvula "
"está a la misma elevación que el fondo del tanque, entonces :math:`h_{0} = "
"h_{Tank}`. Consulte la figura anterior para distinguir :math:`h_{0}`"
" y :math:`h_{Tank}`."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:37
msgid ""
"We can use the proportionality :math:`Q \\propto \\sqrt{h}`, which applies "
"to both minor losses and orifices to form a relationship between water level"
" in the tank :math:`h` and time :math:`t`. This proportionality comes from "
"rearranging the minor loss Equation :math:`h = K \\frac{Q^2}{2 g A^2}` for "
":math:`Q` instead of :math:`h`. A table of proportionality between :math:`Q`"
" and :math:`h` can be found in :numref:`table_h_Q_proportionality`"
msgstr ""
"Podemos usar la proporcionalidad :math:`Q \\propto \\sqrt{h}`, aplicable tanto "
"a las pérdidas menores como a los orificios, para relacionar el nivel del agua "
"en el tanque :math:`h` con el tiempo :math:`t`. Esta proporcionalidad se obtiene "
"al despejar :math:`Q`, en vez de :math:`h`, de la ecuación de pérdidas menores "
":math:`h = K \\frac{Q^2}{2 g A^2}`. La tabla "
":numref:`table_h_Q_proportionality` muestra la proporcionalidad entre "
":math:`Q` y :math:`h`."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:39
msgid ""
"Using Equation :eq:`Q_tank_with_valve` and this proportionality "
"relationship, we make the following plots. On the left, the valve is at the "
"same elevation as the bottom of the tank, or :math:`h_{Tank} = h_0`. Our "
"attempt to get a continuous flow rate out of this system is to make "
":math:`\\frac{h_{Tank}}{h_0}` very small by elevating the tank far above the"
" valve. On the right, :math:`\\frac{h_{Tank}}{h_0} = \\frac{1}{50}`. While "
"the plot looks great and provides essentially constant head, elevating the "
"tank by 50 times its height is not realistic. The ‘tank with a valve’ is not"
" a solution to the constant head problem."
msgstr ""
"A partir de la ecuación :eq:`Q_tank_with_valve` y de esta relación de "
"proporcionalidad, obtenemos las siguientes gráficas. A la izquierda, la válvula "
"está a la misma elevación que el fondo del tanque, es decir, "
":math:`h_{Tank} = h_0`. Para intentar obtener un caudal continuo, hacemos muy "
"pequeña la relación :math:`\\frac{h_{Tank}}{h_0}` elevando el tanque muy por "
"encima de la válvula. A la derecha, "
":math:`\\frac{h_{Tank}}{h_0} = \\frac{1}{50}`. Aunque la gráfica muestra una "
"carga prácticamente constante, no es realista elevar el tanque a una altura "
"equivalente a 50 veces su propia altura. Por tanto, el 'tanque con válvula' "
"no resuelve el problema de mantener una carga constante."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:47
msgid "Manipulating hypochlorinator heights"
msgstr "Manipulación de las alturas de los hipocloradores"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:47
msgid ""
"These graphs show how manipulation of the variables in the :math:`Q(t)` "
"expression can result in effectively constant head."
msgstr ""
"Estos gráficos muestran cómo la manipulación de las variables en la "
"expresión :math:`Q(t)` puede producir una carga prácticamente constante."

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:53
msgid "Drain System for a Tank"
msgstr "Sistema de desagüe para un depósito"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:54
msgid ""
"While the ‘tank with a valve’ scenario is not a good constant head solution,"
" we can use our understanding of the system to properly design drain systems"
" for AguaClara reactors like flocculators and clarifiers, since they are "
"just tanks with valves. The derivation for the following equation is here, "
"along with more details on AguaClara’s pipe stub method for draining tanks: "
":ref:`heading_diameter_and_time_tank_drain_equation`. The derived ‘Tank "
"Drain’ equation is as follows:"
msgstr ""
"Aunque el escenario del 'tanque con válvula' no es una buena solución para mantener una carga "
"constante, podemos usar nuestro conocimiento del sistema para diseñar "
"correctamente sistemas de drenaje para reactores AguaClara como floculadores"
" y clarificadores, ya que son simplemente tanques con válvulas. La "
"derivación para la siguiente ecuación está aquí, junto con más detalles "
"sobre el método de AguaClara que utiliza un niple para drenar tanques: "
":ref:`heading_diameter_and_time_tank_drain_equation`. La ecuación derivada "
"de drenaje del tanque es la siguiente:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:56
msgid ""
"D_{Pipe} = \\sqrt{ \\frac{8 L_{Tank} W_{Tank}}{\\pi t_{Drain}}} {\\left( "
"\\frac{H_{Tank} \\sum K }{2g} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{4}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:60
msgid ""
"The equation can also be rearranged to solve for the time it would take to "
"drain a tank given its dimensions and a certain drain pipe size:"
msgstr ""
"La ecuación también puede reorganizarse para resolver el tiempo que tardaría"
" en vaciar un tanque, dadas sus dimensiones y un determinado tamaño de "
"tubería de drenaje:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:62
msgid ""
"t_{Drain} =  \\frac{8 L_{Tank} W_{Tank}}{\\pi D_{Pipe}^2} {\\left( "
"\\frac{H_{Tank} \\sum K }{2g} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:66
msgid "Such that:"
msgstr "Tal que:"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:67
msgid ":math:`D_{Pipe}` = Diameter of the drain piping"
msgstr ":math:`D_{Pipe}` = Diámetro de la tubería de desagüe"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:68
msgid ":math:`L_{Tank}, W_{Tank}, H_{Tank}` = Tank dimensions"
msgstr ":math:`L_{Tank}, W_{Tank}, H_{Tank}` = Dimensiones del tanque"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:69
msgid ":math:`t_{Drain}` = Time it takes to drain the tank"
msgstr ":math:`t_{Drain}` = Tiempo que tarda en vaciar el tanque"

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:70
msgid ":math:`\\sum K` = Sum of all the minor loss coefficients in the system"
msgstr ":math:`\\sum K` = Suma de todos los coeficientes de pérdida menor del sistema"

